{"id":"orbital-5d97db","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cStack\u003e` layout component — a vertical flex container that eliminates the most common Tailwind workaround in the codebase.\n\n## Problem\n\nNearly every Card body and page section wraps children in `\u003cdiv class=\"flex flex-col gap-X\"\u003e`. This pattern appears ~20 times in `index.html.orb` alone.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cStack gap=\"4\"\u003e\n  \u003cTextField .../\u003e\n  \u003cTextField .../\u003e\n  \u003cButton\u003eSubmit\u003c/Button\u003e\n\u003c/Stack\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `gap` — spacing between children (Tailwind spacing scale or named sizes)\n- `align` — cross-axis alignment (`start`, `center`, `end`, `stretch`)\n- `padding` — internal padding\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Renders a `\u003cdiv\u003e` with `display: flex; flex-direction: column` and the appropriate gap\n- CSS class: `Orbital-Stack` with `data-gap`, `data-align` attributes\n- Follows existing Orbital conventions (data-attribute-driven styling)","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"a0","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Stack layout component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T11:46:27.064908Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-f335c5","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add an `\u003cInlineStack\u003e` layout component — a horizontal flex container that pairs with `\u003cStack\u003e` to cover virtually all flex usage.\n\n## Problem\n\nHorizontal flex containers like `\u003cdiv class=\"flex items-center gap-2\"\u003e` and `\u003cdiv class=\"flex justify-between\"\u003e` appear ~12 times in `index.html.orb`. Each instance manually specifies alignment and distribution.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cInlineStack gap=\"2\" align=\"center\"\u003e\n  \u003cButton\u003eSave\u003c/Button\u003e\n  \u003cButton variant=\"outline\"\u003eCancel\u003c/Button\u003e\n\u003c/InlineStack\u003e\n\n\u003cInlineStack distribute=\"between\"\u003e\n  \u003cText\u003eLabel\u003c/Text\u003e\n  \u003cText\u003eValue\u003c/Text\u003e\n\u003c/InlineStack\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `gap` — spacing between children (Tailwind spacing scale or named sizes)\n- `align` — cross-axis alignment (`start`, `center`, `end`, `stretch`)\n- `distribute` — main-axis distribution (`start`, `center`, `end`, `between`, `around`, `evenly`)\n- `wrap` — whether children wrap (boolean, default false)\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Renders a `\u003cdiv\u003e` with `display: flex; flex-direction: row` and the appropriate gap\n- CSS class: `Orbital-InlineStack` with `data-gap`, `data-align`, `data-distribute` attributes\n- Together with Stack, these two components would eliminate ~32 raw divs from the index page","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"a1","status":"BACKLOG","title":"InlineStack layout component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T11:46:27.086949Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-45d373","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cGrid\u003e` layout component — a column-based grid container that replaces manual `grid grid-cols-X gap-X` patterns.\n\n## Problem\n\nRaw `\u003cdiv class=\"grid grid-cols-X gap-X\"\u003e` appears 8 times in `index.html.orb`, used for form field layouts, stat tile rows, menu grids, and the page-level column layout. The payment form (line 60) also needs `col-span` control on children.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cGrid columns=\"2\" gap=\"4\"\u003e\n  \u003cTextField name=\"first_name\" label=\"First Name\"/\u003e\n  \u003cTextField name=\"last_name\" label=\"Last Name\"/\u003e\n\u003c/Grid\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- with span control --\u003e\n\u003cGrid columns=\"5\" gap=\"4\"\u003e\n  \u003cGrid:Cell span=\"4\"\u003e\n    \u003cTextField name=\"card_number\" label=\"Card number\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/Grid:Cell\u003e\n  \u003cGrid:Cell\u003e\n    \u003cTextField name=\"ccv\" label=\"CCV\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/Grid:Cell\u003e\n\u003c/Grid\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `columns` — number of columns (integer or responsive hash)\n- `gap` — gap between cells (Tailwind spacing scale or named sizes)\n\n### Slots\n\n- `Grid:Cell` — optional wrapper for children that need span control\n  - `span` — number of columns to span (integer)\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Renders a `\u003cdiv\u003e` with `display: grid` and `grid-template-columns`\n- CSS class: `Orbital-Grid` with `data-columns`, `data-gap` attributes\n- Children without a `Grid:Cell` wrapper occupy one column by default\n- Responsive column counts (e.g. 1 on mobile, 2 on tablet, 4 on desktop) would be a natural follow-up","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"a2","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Grid layout component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T11:49:00.370043Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-4005a9","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `fullwidth` boolean prop to the Button component, matching the convention already established by Select.\n\n## Problem\n\n`\u003cButton class=\"w-full\"\u003e` appears 5 times in `index.html.orb` (lines 188, 332, 349, 351, 487), typically in Card footers. This is a common enough need that it should be a first-class prop rather than a Tailwind override.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cButton fullwidth\u003eSave Preferences\u003c/Button\u003e\n\u003cButton fullwidth variant=\"outline\"\u003eCancel\u003c/Button\u003e\n```\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Add `attribute :fullwidth, :boolean, default: false` to `Button`\n- Emit `data-fullwidth` attribute when true\n- Add CSS: `\u0026[data-fullwidth] { @apply w-full; }` to `button.css`\n- Follows the same pattern as `Select`, which already has `fullwidth`","labels":["improvement"],"sort_order":"a3","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Add fullwidth prop to Button"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T11:50:15.99813Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-cd7cf2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `dot` prop to Badge that renders a small colored circle, replacing hand-rolled status dot markup.\n\n## Problem\n\nStatus dots inside Badge are currently built with raw HTML and hardcoded colors:\n\n```html\n\u003cBadge variant=\"outline\" class=\"w-fit\"\u003e\n  \u003cspan class=\"inline-block w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-yellow-400 mr-1.5\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n  Pending Setup\n\u003c/Badge\u003e\n```\n\nThis bypasses the design system's tone tokens and won't adapt to dark mode.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cBadge dot=\"warning\"\u003ePending Setup\u003c/Badge\u003e\n\u003cBadge dot=\"success\"\u003eActive\u003c/Badge\u003e\n\u003cBadge dot=\"danger\"\u003eFailed\u003c/Badge\u003e\n```\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Add `attribute :dot, :symbol, default: nil, only: [:default, :success, :warning, :danger, :info, :subdued]`\n- When present, render a `\u003cspan class=\"Orbital-Badge-Dot\" data-tone=\"...\"\u003e` before the content\n- Dot styling: small circle (w-2 h-2), color driven by tone tokens (same semantic color system as Text tone)\n- Spacing between dot and content handled by the component, not the consumer","labels":["improvement"],"sort_order":"a4","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Add dot prop to Badge for status indicators"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T11:51:18.363181Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-4c9dcb","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add an `icon` prop to Badge for built-in icon placement with proper spacing and tinting, similar to how Menu:Item handles icons.\n\n## Problem\n\nIcons inside Badge require manual color and spacing overrides:\n\n```html\n\u003cBadge variant=\"secondary\"\u003e\n  \u003cIcon name=\"check-circle\" size=\"sm\" class=\"text-green-500 mr-1\"/\u003e\n  Successful\n\u003c/Badge\u003e\n\n\u003cBadge variant=\"outline\"\u003e\n  \u003cIcon name=\"clock\" size=\"sm\" class=\"text-gray-500 mr-1\"/\u003e\n  Scheduled\n\u003c/Badge\u003e\n```\n\nThe `mr-1` spacing and hardcoded color classes are workarounds. The colors also won't adapt to dark mode.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cBadge icon=\"check-circle\" tone=\"success\"\u003eSuccessful\u003c/Badge\u003e\n\u003cBadge icon=\"clock\" tone=\"subdued\"\u003eScheduled\u003c/Badge\u003e\n```\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Add `attribute :icon, :any, default: nil` — accepts an icon name string (include `IconProp` concern, same as Menu:Item)\n- Add `attribute :tone, :symbol, default: nil, only: [:success, :warning, :danger, :info, :subdued]`\n- When `icon` is present, render an Icon before the content with appropriate size (sm) and spacing\n- Icon color derived from `tone` using the existing semantic color tokens\n- Tone could also tint the badge background/border subtly, but that's a design decision for implementation time","labels":["improvement"],"sort_order":"a5","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Add icon prop to Badge"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T11:51:25.630089Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-33ae5a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add `gap` and `padding` props to Card's content area, with sensible defaults that reduce the need for inner wrapper divs.\n\n## Problem\n\nAlmost every Card body wraps its children in `\u003cdiv class=\"flex flex-col gap-X\"\u003e` to get vertical spacing. This pattern appears ~7 times in `index.html.orb` alone. Card's `.Orbital-Card-Content` already has padding (`p-6 pt-0`) but no way to control child spacing.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003c!-- explicit gap --\u003e\n\u003cCard gap=\"4\"\u003e\n  \u003cTextField .../\u003e\n  \u003cTextField .../\u003e\n  \u003cButton\u003eSubmit\u003c/Button\u003e\n\u003c/Card\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- tighter padding for compact cards --\u003e\n\u003cCard gap=\"2\" padding=\"4\"\u003e\n  ...\n\u003c/Card\u003e\n```\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Add `attribute :gap, :any, default: nil` — spacing between direct children in the content area\n- Add `attribute :padding, :any, default: nil` — override content area padding\n- Pass these down to `.Orbital-Card-Content` via `data-gap` / `data-padding` attributes or inline styles\n- Consider a reasonable default gap (e.g. `4`) so most Cards just work without specifying it\n- The existing `p-6 pt-0` padding on Card-Content becomes the default when `padding` is not set","labels":["improvement"],"sort_order":"a6","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Add gap and padding props to Card"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T11:51:49.086143Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-2fc7af","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add an `\u003cEmptyState\u003e` component for the common pattern of a centered placeholder with icon, heading, description, and action.\n\n## Problem\n\nEmpty/placeholder states are manually constructed with 10–15 lines of layout Tailwind each time. Two distinct instances appear in `index.html.orb` (lines 222–234 and 362–371), and the pattern will recur across any app using Orbital.\n\n## Context: two rendering contexts\n\nEmptyState can appear:\n\n1. **Inside a Card** — the Card provides the container (border, background, shadow). EmptyState should only handle its own internal layout, not add a redundant border.\n2. **Standalone on a page** — EmptyState needs its own container treatment (e.g. dashed border for a drop zone or upload prompt, or a subtle background).\n\nThe component must work cleanly in both contexts without the consumer needing to compensate.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003c!-- Inside a Card (no container of its own) --\u003e\n\u003cCard\u003e\n  \u003cEmptyState icon=\"plus\" heading=\"No items yet\"\n              description=\"Create your first item to get started.\"\u003e\n    \u003cButton variant=\"outline\"\u003eCreate Item\u003c/Button\u003e\n  \u003c/EmptyState\u003e\n\u003c/Card\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- Standalone with dashed border --\u003e\n\u003cEmptyState bordered icon=\"upload\" heading=\"Drop files here\"\n            description=\"Or click to browse.\"\u003e\n  \u003cButton\u003eBrowse Files\u003c/Button\u003e\n\u003c/EmptyState\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- Processing/loading variant --\u003e\n\u003cEmptyState\u003e\n  \u003cSpinner/\u003e\n  \u003cEmptyState:Heading\u003eProcessing your request\u003c/EmptyState:Heading\u003e\n  \u003cEmptyState:Description\u003ePlease wait...\u003c/EmptyState:Description\u003e\n  \u003cButton variant=\"secondary\"\u003eCancel\u003c/Button\u003e\n\u003c/EmptyState\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `icon` — icon name, rendered inside a muted circle (`rounded-full bg-muted p-3`)\n- `heading` — primary text (string shorthand)\n- `description` — supporting text (string shorthand)\n- `bordered` — adds a border container (boolean, default false); use `dashed` variant for upload/drop zones\n\n### Slots\n\n- Default content slot — for action buttons or custom content below the description\n- `EmptyState:Heading` — override for when heading needs rich content\n- `EmptyState:Description` — override for when description needs rich content\n\n### Design decisions to resolve during implementation\n\n- Should `bordered` default to dashed or solid? Or separate `dashed` boolean?\n- Icon circle size: should it scale with a `size` prop on EmptyState, or stay fixed?\n- Vertical padding: needs to feel proportional whether inside a compact Card or filling a full page section","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"a7","status":"BACKLOG","title":"EmptyState component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T11:53:08.390034Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-b5304c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cDataList\u003e` component for displaying key-value pairs in a bordered, divided list.\n\n## Problem\n\nLabel–value row lists are built with 14+ lines of structural Tailwind — bordered container, `divide-y`, manual padding, and `justify-between` on every row (e.g. `index.html.orb` lines 124–137). This is a common pattern in financial summaries, settings pages, and detail views.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cDataList\u003e\n  \u003cDataList:Row label=\"Net Royalties\" value=\"$1,248.75\"/\u003e\n  \u003cDataList:Row label=\"Processing Fee\" value=\"-$37.46\"/\u003e\n  \u003cDataList:Row label=\"Total Ready to Claim\" value=\"$1,211.29 USD\" summary/\u003e\n\u003c/DataList\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- with tone for highlighting --\u003e\n\u003cDataList\u003e\n  \u003cDataList:Row label=\"Status\" value=\"Overdue\" tone=\"danger\"/\u003e\n  \u003cDataList:Row label=\"Payment\" value=\"Received\" tone=\"success\"/\u003e\n  \u003cDataList:Row label=\"Total\" value=\"$500.00\" summary/\u003e\n\u003c/DataList\u003e\n```\n\n### DataList props\n\n- Renders a bordered, rounded container with divided rows\n- No props needed on the container initially — keep it simple\n\n### DataList:Row props\n\n- `label` — left-side text (string)\n- `value` — right-side text (string)\n- `tone` — semantic background tint: `warning`, `danger`, `success`, `info` (symbol, default nil). Uses the existing semantic color tokens for subtle background coloring.\n- `summary` — boolean (default false). Applies a grey `bg-muted/50` background and bold text formatting, intended for totals/summary rows.\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Container: `border rounded-lg divide-y` with overflow hidden\n- Rows: flex with `justify-between`, consistent `px-4 py-3` padding\n- `tone` and `summary` are independent — a row could be both a summary and have a tone\n- Text sizing defaults to `sm` to match typical data-dense usage","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"a8","status":"BACKLOG","title":"DataList component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T11:54:38.870895Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-ec2a34","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cStatTile\u003e` component for the recurring pattern of a muted-background tile with an eyebrow label, prominent value, and optional supporting content.\n\n## Problem\n\nMuted-background stat tiles are manually built with `\u003cdiv class=\"flex flex-col p-4 gap-2 bg-muted/50 rounded-md\"\u003e` plus individual Text/Heading children. This pattern appears 4 times in `index.html.orb` (lines 176–180, 181–185, 304–312, 314–321) in both compact info-tile and larger metric-with-progress variants.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003c!-- Simple info tile --\u003e\n\u003cStatTile label=\"Upcoming\" value=\"May 2024\" supporting=\"Scheduled\"/\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- With rich content (e.g. a ProgressBar below the value) --\u003e\n\u003cStatTile label=\"Retirement\" value=\"$410,000\"\u003e\n  \u003cProgressBar value=273000 max=410000/\u003e\n\u003c/StatTile\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `label` — eyebrow text above the value (rendered small, uppercase, tracked)\n- `value` — the prominent metric or text (rendered as a Heading)\n- `supporting` — optional supporting text below value/content (string shorthand, rendered as subdued Text)\n\n### Slots\n\n- Default content slot — for rich content between the value and supporting text (e.g. ProgressBar, custom annotations)\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Container: muted background, rounded, padded, vertical flex with small gap\n- Label inherits `uppercase tracking-wider` treatment by default\n- Value rendered at a prominent heading size\n- Two implicit sizes may emerge (compact vs standard) but start with one and see if a `size` prop is needed later","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"a9","status":"BACKLOG","title":"StatTile component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T11:57:09.279679Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-61bcb5","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cLink\u003e` component for inline text links with consistent styling from theme tokens.\n\n## Problem\n\nRaw `\u003ca\u003e` tags with hardcoded colors bypass the design system. In `index.html.orb`, line 505 uses `\u003ca href=\"#\" class=\"text-blue-800 text-body-sm\"\u003eForgot?\u003c/a\u003e` — `text-blue-800` won't adapt to dark mode. This is the exact kind of bug a Link component prevents.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cLink url=\"/forgot\"\u003eForgot password?\u003c/Link\u003e\n\u003cLink url=\"/components\"\u003eView all components\u003c/Link\u003e\n\u003cLink external url=\"https://github.com/...\"\u003eSource on GitHub\u003c/Link\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `url` — href target (string, default `\"#\"`)\n- `external` — opens in a new tab/window via `target=\"_blank\"` with `rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"` (boolean, default false)\n\n### Open design question\n\n- Should `external` automatically render a small external-link icon after the text? Arguments for: it's a common accessibility/UX convention that signals navigation away from the site. Arguments against: it adds visual noise and the consumer can always add an Icon manually. Decide during implementation.\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Renders an `\u003ca\u003e` tag with `Orbital-Link` class\n- Color, hover state, underline behavior, and focus ring all derived from theme tokens\n- Should work well both standalone and inline within Text or other components\n- Dark mode safe by default — no hardcoded color values","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"aA","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Link component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T11:58:29.575344Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-5d97db","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cStack\u003e` layout component — a vertical flex container that eliminates the most common Tailwind workaround in the codebase.\n\n## Problem\n\nNearly every Card body and page section wraps children in `\u003cdiv class=\"flex flex-col gap-X\"\u003e`. This pattern appears ~20 times in `index.html.orb` alone.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cStack gap=\"4\"\u003e\n  \u003cTextField .../\u003e\n  \u003cTextField .../\u003e\n  \u003cButton\u003eSubmit\u003c/Button\u003e\n\u003c/Stack\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- with dividers between children --\u003e\n\u003cStack gap=\"4\" dividers\u003e\n  \u003cCheckBox name=\"notif_transactions\" label=\"Transaction alerts\"\n           help=\"Deposits, withdrawals...\" checked/\u003e\n  \u003cCheckBox name=\"notif_security\" label=\"Security alerts\"\n           help=\"Login attempts...\" checked/\u003e\n\u003c/Stack\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `gap` — spacing between children (Tailwind spacing scale or named sizes)\n- `align` — cross-axis alignment (`start`, `center`, `end`, `stretch`)\n- `padding` — internal padding\n- `dividers` — renders a visual separator between each child (boolean, default false). Replaces the `divide-y` pattern used for option lists, notification settings, etc. (e.g. `index.html.orb` lines 472–485). This eliminates the need for a separate OptionList component for pure layout purposes.\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Renders a `\u003cdiv\u003e` with `display: flex; flex-direction: column` and the appropriate gap\n- CSS class: `Orbital-Stack` with `data-gap`, `data-align` attributes\n- Follows existing Orbital conventions (data-attribute-driven styling)\n- When `dividers` is true, render `Orbital-Separator` elements between children or use CSS `border-bottom` / `divide-y` on the container","priority":1},"created_at":"2026-07-27T12:20:09.953248Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-3139b6","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cTabs\u003e` component — a set of layered content panels that are displayed one at a time, switched by tab triggers.\n\n## Rationale\n\nTabs are one of the most common UI patterns for organizing content into switchable sections (settings pages, detail views, dashboards). Orbital currently has no equivalent.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cTabs default=\"general\"\u003e\n  \u003cTabs:List\u003e\n    \u003cTabs:Trigger value=\"general\"\u003eGeneral\u003c/Tabs:Trigger\u003e\n    \u003cTabs:Trigger value=\"security\"\u003eSecurity\u003c/Tabs:Trigger\u003e\n    \u003cTabs:Trigger value=\"notifications\"\u003eNotifications\u003c/Tabs:Trigger\u003e\n  \u003c/Tabs:List\u003e\n  \u003cTabs:Panel value=\"general\"\u003e\n    ...general settings content...\n  \u003c/Tabs:Panel\u003e\n  \u003cTabs:Panel value=\"security\"\u003e\n    ...security settings content...\n  \u003c/Tabs:Panel\u003e\n  \u003cTabs:Panel value=\"notifications\"\u003e\n    ...notification settings content...\n  \u003c/Tabs:Panel\u003e\n\u003c/Tabs\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `default` — value of the initially active tab\n- Tabs:Trigger: `value`, `disabled`, `icon`\n- Tabs:Panel: `value`\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Stimulus controller for tab switching, keyboard navigation (arrow keys), ARIA roles\n- Tab list should support horizontal and vertical orientations\n- Consider whether Tabs can work with Turbo Frames for lazy-loading panel content","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"aB","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Tabs component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T12:05:55.265022Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-8c907e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cTable\u003e` component for displaying tabular data with consistent styling and responsive behavior.\n\n## Rationale\n\nData tables are ubiquitous in web apps — user lists, transaction history, admin panels. A styled Table component ensures consistent typography, alignment, borders, and responsive overflow handling without Tailwind overrides.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cTable\u003e\n  \u003cTable:Header\u003e\n    \u003cTable:Row\u003e\n      \u003cTable:Head\u003eName\u003c/Table:Head\u003e\n      \u003cTable:Head\u003eAmount\u003c/Table:Head\u003e\n      \u003cTable:Head\u003eStatus\u003c/Table:Head\u003e\n    \u003c/Table:Row\u003e\n  \u003c/Table:Header\u003e\n  \u003cTable:Body\u003e\n    \u003cTable:Row\u003e\n      \u003cTable:Cell\u003eInvoice #001\u003c/Table:Cell\u003e\n      \u003cTable:Cell\u003e$250.00\u003c/Table:Cell\u003e\n      \u003cTable:Cell\u003e\u003cBadge dot=\"success\"\u003ePaid\u003c/Badge\u003e\u003c/Table:Cell\u003e\n    \u003c/Table:Row\u003e\n  \u003c/Table:Body\u003e\n\u003c/Table\u003e\n```\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Renders semantic `\u003ctable\u003e`, `\u003cthead\u003e`, `\u003ctbody\u003e`, `\u003ctr\u003e`, `\u003cth\u003e`, `\u003ctd\u003e` elements\n- Wraps in an `overflow-x: auto` container for responsive horizontal scrolling\n- `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` on numeric columns\n- Striped rows, hover states, and compact/default size variants\n- Slot-based composition — not data-driven. Keeps it simple and composable with any content.","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"aC","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Table component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T12:06:01.966746Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-5131dd","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cToast\u003e` component for transient feedback messages that appear temporarily and dismiss automatically.\n\n## Rationale\n\nToasts are the standard way to confirm actions (save, delete, send) or surface errors without blocking the user. Orbital currently has Alert (modal) but nothing for non-blocking transient notifications.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003c!-- Declarative trigger via Stimulus/Turbo --\u003e\n\u003cToast tone=\"success\" title=\"Changes saved\"\n       description=\"Your preferences have been updated.\"/\u003e\n\n\u003cToast tone=\"danger\" title=\"Upload failed\"\n       description=\"File exceeds the 10MB limit.\"/\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `tone` — `success`, `warning`, `danger`, `info`, `default` (drives icon and color)\n- `title` — primary message text\n- `description` — optional secondary text\n- `duration` — auto-dismiss time in ms (default ~5000, 0 for persistent)\n- `dismissible` — show close button (boolean, default true)\n- `action` — optional action button text + handler\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Needs a toast container/portal (fixed position, typically bottom-right or top-right)\n- Stimulus controller for lifecycle (appear, auto-dismiss, manual dismiss)\n- Stack multiple toasts with consistent spacing\n- Consider integration with Turbo Stream for server-triggered toasts\n- Entry/exit animations with `prefers-reduced-motion` respect","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"aD","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Toast component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T12:06:09.671742Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-7857fd","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cSwitch\u003e` component — a toggle control for binary on/off states, visually distinct from CheckBox.\n\n## Rationale\n\nSwitch and CheckBox serve different UX roles: switches represent an immediate state change (enable/disable a feature), while checkboxes represent a selection to be submitted. Orbital has CheckBox but no Switch.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cSwitch name=\"dark_mode\" label=\"Dark mode\"/\u003e\n\u003cSwitch name=\"notifications\" label=\"Push notifications\"\n        help=\"Receive alerts on your device\" checked/\u003e\n\u003cSwitch name=\"maintenance\" label=\"Maintenance mode\" disabled/\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `name` — form input name\n- `label` — visible label text\n- `help` — optional help text below the label\n- `checked` — initial state (boolean, default false)\n- `disabled` — (boolean, default false)\n- `size` — `sm`, `default`, `lg`\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Renders a styled toggle track with a sliding thumb\n- Hidden checkbox input for form compatibility\n- Stimulus controller for toggle behavior\n- ARIA `role=\"switch\"` with `aria-checked`\n- Follows the same label/help/error pattern as CheckBox and TextField","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"aE","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Switch component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T12:06:15.231582Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-5aecdf","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cSkeleton\u003e` component for displaying placeholder shapes while content is loading.\n\n## Rationale\n\nSkeleton screens are the modern standard for loading states — they reduce perceived load time and prevent layout shift. Orbital has Spinner for indeterminate loading but nothing for content-shaped placeholders.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003c!-- Basic shapes --\u003e\n\u003cSkeleton width=\"200px\" height=\"20px\"/\u003e\n\u003cSkeleton width=\"48px\" height=\"48px\" circle/\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- Compose to match a card layout --\u003e\n\u003cCard\u003e\n  \u003cStack gap=\"4\"\u003e\n    \u003cSkeleton width=\"60%\" height=\"20px\"/\u003e\n    \u003cSkeleton width=\"100%\" height=\"14px\"/\u003e\n    \u003cSkeleton width=\"80%\" height=\"14px\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/Stack\u003e\n\u003c/Card\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `width` — CSS width (string, default `\"100%\"`)\n- `height` — CSS height (string, default `\"1rem\"`)\n- `circle` — renders as a circle (boolean, default false)\n- `rounded` — border radius (boolean or string, default true)\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Subtle pulsing animation (`@keyframes` with opacity or shimmer gradient)\n- Respects `prefers-reduced-motion` (disable or reduce animation)\n- Uses `bg-muted` or similar token for the placeholder color\n- Should be simple and composable — not prescriptive about layouts","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"aF","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Skeleton component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T12:06:21.45619Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-a44bc1","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cBreadcrumb\u003e` component for displaying hierarchical navigation paths.\n\n## Rationale\n\nBreadcrumbs are standard navigation for multi-level apps — admin panels, documentation, e-commerce. They help users understand where they are and navigate back up the hierarchy.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cBreadcrumb\u003e\n  \u003cBreadcrumb:Item url=\"/dashboard\"\u003eDashboard\u003c/Breadcrumb:Item\u003e\n  \u003cBreadcrumb:Item url=\"/projects\"\u003eProjects\u003c/Breadcrumb:Item\u003e\n  \u003cBreadcrumb:Item\u003eSettings\u003c/Breadcrumb:Item\u003e\n\u003c/Breadcrumb\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- Breadcrumb:Item: `url` (string, nil for current/last item), `icon` (optional leading icon)\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Renders a `\u003cnav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"\u003e` with an `\u003col\u003e` list\n- Automatic separator (chevron or slash) between items via CSS pseudo-elements\n- Last item rendered as plain text (no link), styled differently to indicate current page\n- Subdued, small text styling — breadcrumbs should be unobtrusive\n- Truncation/collapse behavior for long paths could be a follow-up","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"aG","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Breadcrumb component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T12:06:27.605519Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-f453cf","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cRadioGroup\u003e` component — a set of mutually exclusive options where only one can be selected at a time.\n\n## Rationale\n\nRadio buttons are a fundamental form control for single-selection from a small set of options. Orbital has CheckBox but no radio equivalent. This was identified during the OptionList discussion — selection management needs its own component rather than being bolted onto a layout primitive.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cRadioGroup name=\"plan\" label=\"Select a plan\"\u003e\n  \u003cRadioGroup:Option value=\"free\" label=\"Free\"\n                     help=\"Up to 3 projects\"/\u003e\n  \u003cRadioGroup:Option value=\"pro\" label=\"Pro\"\n                     help=\"Unlimited projects, priority support\"/\u003e\n  \u003cRadioGroup:Option value=\"enterprise\" label=\"Enterprise\"\n                     help=\"Custom limits, SLA, dedicated support\" disabled/\u003e\n\u003c/RadioGroup\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `name` — form input name\n- `label` — group label\n- `default` — initially selected value\n- `orientation` — `vertical` (default) or `horizontal`\n- RadioGroup:Option: `value`, `label`, `help`, `disabled`\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Renders native `\u003cinput type=\"radio\"\u003e` elements for form compatibility\n- Stimulus controller for keyboard navigation (arrow keys cycle through options)\n- ARIA `role=\"radiogroup\"` on container\n- Follows the same label/help/error pattern as CheckBox and TextField\n- Visual style should complement CheckBox (similar sizing, label placement)","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"aH","status":"BACKLOG","title":"RadioGroup component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T12:06:33.65758Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-685742","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cPagination\u003e` component for navigating through paged content.\n\n## Rationale\n\nPagination pairs naturally with Table and any list view. In `index.html.orb` (lines 255–266), pagination is currently hand-built with individual Buttons and ButtonGroups. A dedicated component would handle page numbering, truncation, and navigation consistently.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cPagination current=2 total=24 url=\"/items?page=:page\"/\u003e\n\n\u003c!-- or slot-based for custom rendering --\u003e\n\u003cPagination current=2 total=24\u003e\n  \u003cPagination:Previous url=\"/items?page=1\"/\u003e\n  \u003cPagination:Pages/\u003e\n  \u003cPagination:Next url=\"/items?page=3\"/\u003e\n\u003c/Pagination\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `current` — current page number\n- `total` — total number of pages\n- `url` — URL template with `:page` placeholder for simple link-based pagination\n- `siblings` — number of page links shown around current (default 1)\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Renders prev/next buttons + page number links with ellipsis truncation for large page counts\n- Uses `\u003cnav aria-label=\"Pagination\"\u003e` with proper ARIA\n- Current page visually distinct (not a link)\n- Composes Button/ButtonGroup internally for consistent styling\n- Should work with both full page navigation and Turbo Frames","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"aI","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Pagination component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T12:06:41.297606Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-c055be","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cSheet\u003e` component — a slide-out panel that overlays from the edge of the screen.\n\n## Rationale\n\nOrbital has Modal and Dialog for centered overlays, but nothing for side panels. Sheets are the standard pattern for mobile navigation, detail views, filters, and forms that need more space than a popover but less interruption than a full modal.\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cSheet side=\"right\"\u003e\n  \u003cSheet:Header\u003e\n    \u003cHeader:Title\u003eEdit Profile\u003c/Header:Title\u003e\n    \u003cHeader:Description\u003eMake changes to your profile.\u003c/Header:Description\u003e\n  \u003c/Sheet:Header\u003e\n  \u003cSheet:Body\u003e\n    \u003cStack gap=\"4\"\u003e\n      \u003cTextField name=\"name\" label=\"Name\"/\u003e\n      \u003cTextField name=\"email\" label=\"Email\"/\u003e\n    \u003c/Stack\u003e\n  \u003c/Sheet:Body\u003e\n  \u003cSheet:Footer\u003e\n    \u003cButton fullwidth\u003eSave Changes\u003c/Button\u003e\n  \u003c/Sheet:Footer\u003e\n\u003c/Sheet\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `side` — which edge it slides from: `left`, `right` (default), `top`, `bottom`\n- `open` — whether the sheet is visible (boolean, default false)\n- `dismissible` — show close button and allow backdrop click to close (boolean, default true)\n- `size` — width/height of the panel: `sm`, `default`, `lg`, `full`\n\n### Slots\n\n- `Sheet:Header` (with Title, Description sub-slots, mirroring Dialog)\n- `Sheet:Body`\n- `Sheet:Footer`\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Shares infrastructure with Modal/Dialog (backdrop, focus trap, scroll lock, Stimulus controller)\n- Slide-in/out animation with `prefers-reduced-motion` respect\n- Backdrop overlay like Modal\n- Could reuse the existing `Orbital::ModalFrame` / Turbo Frame integration pattern","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"aJ","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Sheet component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T12:06:48.655957Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-cf0251","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add a `\u003cSlider\u003e` component — a range input for selecting a numeric value within a given range.\n\n## Rationale\n\nSliders are common in settings (volume, brightness, price range filters) and configuration UIs. A styled Slider component ensures consistency with the rest of the form controls (TextField, Select, CheckBox, Switch).\n\n## Proposed API\n\n```html\n\u003cSlider name=\"volume\" label=\"Volume\" min=0 max=100 value=75/\u003e\n\u003cSlider name=\"price_range\" label=\"Price Range\"\n        min=0 max=1000 step=10 value=250\n        help=\"Filter results by maximum price\"/\u003e\n\u003cSlider name=\"opacity\" label=\"Opacity\" min=0 max=1 step=0.01/\u003e\n```\n\n### Props\n\n- `name` — form input name\n- `label` — visible label\n- `min` — minimum value (default 0)\n- `max` — maximum value (default 100)\n- `step` — step increment (default 1)\n- `value` — current value\n- `disabled` — (boolean, default false)\n- `help` — optional help text\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- Custom-styled track and thumb over a native `\u003cinput type=\"range\"\u003e` for form compatibility\n- Stimulus controller for value display and optional keyboard fine-tuning\n- Track fill color to visually indicate the selected portion\n- Follows the same label/help/error pattern as other form controls\n- Range selection (two thumbs) could be a follow-up enhancement","labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"aK","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Slider component"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T12:06:54.690426Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-2b7ca2","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Swap the icon source from FontAwesome Free to Lucide, keeping the existing server-side inline SVG rendering approach.\n\n## Rationale\n\nFontAwesome Free has a limited icon set and inconsistent coverage across variants. Lucide (the icon set ShadCN uses) offers ~1500 clean, cohesive stroke-based icons under MIT license. Since Orbital already follows ShadCN conventions, Lucide is a natural fit.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Replace the SVG source files with Lucide's icon set\n- Update `Orbital::Icons.render` to read from the new source\n- Map all existing FontAwesome icon names to their Lucide equivalents across the library and demo app\n- Update the Icon component documentation page\n\n## Key considerations\n\n### Stroke-only\nLucide is stroke-only (consistent 2px stroke, no solid/filled variants). The current Icon component supports `variant: [:solid, :regular, :brands]`:\n- **solid/regular** — the distinction goes away. Most UI usage works fine with stroke style. Audit existing `variant=\"solid\"` usage to confirm nothing relies on the filled appearance for legibility.\n- **brands** — Lucide does not include brand logos (GitHub, Slack, etc.). These need a separate solution — either keep a small set of brand SVGs from another source, or use inline SVGs for the few brand icons needed.\n\n### Icon name mapping\nFontAwesome and Lucide use different naming conventions. A mapping table is needed. Examples:\n- `circle-info` → `info`\n- `gear` → `settings`\n- `arrow-right-from-bracket` → `log-out`\n- `magnifying-glass` → `search`\n- `circle-notch` (spinner) → needs a suitable replacement or custom SVG\n\n### Migration\n- All `.orb` templates and component files referencing icon names need updating\n- The `variant` prop on Icon may be simplified or deprecated\n- Rendering pipeline (`Orbital::Icons.render` → inline SVG) stays unchanged","labels":["improvement"],"sort_order":"aL","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Replace FontAwesome Free icons with Lucide"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T12:16:44.01596Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"orbital-2b7ca2","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Swap the icon source from FontAwesome Free to Lucide, keeping the existing server-side inline SVG rendering approach.\n\n## Rationale\n\nFontAwesome Free has a limited icon set and inconsistent coverage across variants. Lucide (the icon set ShadCN uses) offers ~1500 clean, cohesive stroke-based icons under MIT license. Since Orbital already follows ShadCN conventions, Lucide is a natural fit.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Replace the SVG source files with Lucide's icon set for all UI icons\n- Keep FontAwesome brand SVGs for logo icons (GitHub, Slack, etc.)\n- Update `Orbital::Icons.render` to route `variant=\"brands\"` to FontAwesome source and everything else to Lucide\n- Map all existing FontAwesome icon names to their Lucide equivalents across the library and demo app\n- Update the Icon component documentation page\n\n## Key considerations\n\n### Stroke-only\nLucide is stroke-only (consistent 2px stroke, no solid/filled variants). The current Icon component supports `variant: [:solid, :regular, :brands]`:\n- **solid/regular** — the distinction goes away. Most UI usage works fine with stroke style. Audit existing `variant=\"solid\"` usage to confirm nothing relies on the filled appearance for legibility.\n- **brands** — keep FontAwesome brand SVGs as-is. The Icon component routes `variant=\"brands\"` to the FontAwesome source, everything else to Lucide. Clean separation.\n\n### Icon name mapping\nFontAwesome and Lucide use different naming conventions. A mapping table is needed. Examples:\n- `circle-info` → `info`\n- `gear` → `settings`\n- `arrow-right-from-bracket` → `log-out`\n- `magnifying-glass` → `search`\n- `circle-notch` (spinner) → needs a suitable replacement or custom SVG\n\n### Migration\n- All `.orb` templates and component files referencing icon names need updating\n- The `variant` prop on Icon simplifies to `:default` (Lucide) and `:brands` (FontAwesome)\n- Rendering pipeline (`Orbital::Icons.render` → inline SVG) stays unchanged"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T12:17:24.380879Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.220 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@kuy.io\u003e","source":"mcp"}
